218: /// Compact-window correction (post Live UX Repair): the Live UX Repair
219: /// above deliberately made Compact fill the entire window rather than
220: /// float a small fixed-size card, on the User's direct live-testing
221: /// instruction. A later direct instruction reversed this: Compact must
222: /// again be a genuinely small, fixed-size companion window - but unlike
223: /// the original Frozen Blueprint Â§4.4 text (a floating card *inside* the
224: /// still full-size window, with a dimming scrim), this now resizes the
225: /// real OS window itself down to a small fixed size (see
226: /// services/platform_window_controller.dart), then restores it on
227: /// Expand. [CompactOverlay] itself is unchanged - it still fills
228: /// whatever the actual window is, which is now correct precisely
229: /// because the real window becomes small.
230: class UriHome extends StatefulWidget {
231:   const UriHome({
232:     super.key,
233:     this.filePicker,
234:     this.attachmentOpener,
235:     this.onCompactModeChanged,
